@startuml UserSubmitsResource
' --- DIAGRAM METADATA ---
title "Sequence Diagram: User Submits a New Resource"

' --- PARTICIPANTS ---
actor User
participant "Frontend (Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "Backend (FastAPI)" as Backend

' --- INITIAL STATE ---
ref over User, Frontend, Backend : User is on the Subject Detail page and authenticated.

' --- FLOW OF EVENTS ---
User -> Frontend: Clicks "Add Content", then selects "Suggest a new resource"
activate Frontend
Frontend --> User: Displays Resource Submission Form (title, link_url, description)

User -> Frontend: Fills in the form fields.
User -> Frontend: Clicks "Submit for Review" button
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Backend: POST /subjects/{subjectId}/suggest-resource \n { title: "...", link_url: "...", description: "..." }
note right of Frontend: Auth token with user_id is sent automatically.
activate Backend

Backend -> Backend: Calls crud.create_resource_submission(data, subject_id, user_id)
note right of Backend: Creates a Resource record with status = 'pending'.

Backend --> Frontend: 201 Created [New Resource Object]
deactivate Backend

Frontend --> User: Shows "Submission successful!" message and closes modal.
deactivate Frontend

' --- LINK TO NEXT JOURNEY ---
ref over User, Frontend, Backend : The new resource is now in the review queue for an Admin.

@enduml